**Narrowing this PR (FC, an engineering call).** Keep it to the parts that are solid, and land those:
- relations reach the router;
- code counts verdicts and detects revisions (highest `Revision N`);
- when no reply follows the latest verdict, code settles the route;
- the fix-round brief is switched on by code;
- D1 and D2;
- the fixtures and tests.

**Any reply after a verdict goes to the router as text,** and the router reads it, as it reads the rest of the thread. Replies are language, and the model is the right reader for them. Remove the word-list go/hold classifier and the rule that any Request Changes routes to `implementation`.

The routing-only steer names a stage only when code has settled the route; otherwise it adds none.

Finish by publishing the pass-bar results (HEAD vs PR, on the router model the workspace uses), updating the PR body, and posting a short ticket comment.

